                    }
            %p
              From the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+identities"} simplicial identities
              one finds that the boundary of the
              = succeed "-simplex" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi n
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_n \theta
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
              is constant on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi n
                    %mi θ
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi i
                    %mi θ
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_i d_{n} \theta = d_{n-1} d_i \theta = x
            %p
              So
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi n
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_n \theta
              represents an element in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(X,x)
              and we define a product operation on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(X,x)
              by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi n
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [f]\cdot [g] \coloneqq [d_n \theta]
                    \\,.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine96"} Goerss-Jardine 96, p. 26
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              All the degenerate
              = succeed "-simplices" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi i
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_{0 \leq i \leq n-2}
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOnSimplicialHomotopyGroups"}
              are just there so that the gluing of the two
              = succeed "-cells" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              to each other can be regarded as forming the boundary of an
              = succeed "-simplex" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi n
                      %mi θ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_n \theta
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              The product on homotopy group elements in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOnSimplicialHomotopyGroups"}
              is well defined, in that it is independent of the choice of representatives
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              and of the extension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi θ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
          %p
            e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine96"}> Goerss-Jardine 96, lemma 7.1
            )
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              The product operation in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOnSimplicialHomotopyGroups"}
              yields a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              structure on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(X,x)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
          %p
            e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine96"}> Goerss-Jardine 96, theorem 7.2
            )
          %p Finally:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              The simplicial homotopy groups of any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrant+replacements"} Kan fibrant replacements
              according to def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnderlyingSetsOfSimplicialHomotopyGroups"}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The first homotopy group,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X,x)
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_topological_homotopy_groups Relation to topological homotopy groups
          %p
            The simplicial homotopy groups of a Kan complex coincide with the homotopy groups of its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine96"} Goerss-Jardine 96, page 60
          %h3#relation_to_homotopy_equivalence Relation to homotopy equivalence
          %p
            A morphism of simplicial sets which induces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            on all simplicial homotopy groups is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
            then it is actually a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
          %h3#relation_to_chain_homology_groups_of_associated_moore_complexes Relation to chain homology groups of associated Moore complexes
          %p
            Another way to get the group structure on the homotopy groups of a Kan complex,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan+loop+groupoid"} Dwyer-Kan loop groupoid
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+groupoid"} simplicially enriched groupoid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(X)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %em reduced
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
            is a singleton, and thus that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(X)
            is a simplicial group.)
          %p
            The construction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(X)
            is then given by the free group functor on the various levels, shifted by 1, and with a twist in the zeroth face map (see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dwyer-Kan+loop+groupoid"} Dwyer-Kan loop groupoid
            and simplify to the reduced case.)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              There is an isomorphism between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(X)
              as defined above and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{n-1}(N G(X))
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
              of the simplicial group,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(X)
          %h3#long_exact_sequences_of_a_kan_fibration Long exact sequences of a Kan fibration
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X_0
            any vertex, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \coloneqq f(x) \in Y
            its image and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi x
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_x \coloneqq f^{-1}(y)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            at that point, then the induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of simplicial homotopy groups form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequence of homotopy groups
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots
                  \\to
                  \\pi_{n+1}(Y,y)
                  \\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\pi_n(F,x)
                  \\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\pi_n(X,x)
                  \\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\pi_n(Y,y)
                  \\stackrel{}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\pi_{n-1}(F,x)
                  \\to
                  \\cdots
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots
                  \\to
                  \\pi_1(F,x) \longrightarrow
                  \\pi_0(F) \stackrel{}{\longrightarrow} \pi_0(X) \longrightarrow \pi_0(Y)
          %p
            i.e. a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence"} long exact sequence
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
            ending in a long exact sequence of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+sets"} pointed sets
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine96"} Goerss-Jardine 96, lemma 7.3
          %h2#examples Examples
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_3 Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}(C)
              its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            %p Then
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 0
                        %mi 𝒩
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 \mathcal{N}(C,c)
                  is the set of isomorphism classes of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  with the class of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                  as base point
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 1
                        %mi 𝒩
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1 \mathcal{N}(C,c)
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Aut
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aut_C(c)
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo ≥
                            %mn 2
                        %mi 𝒩
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo ,
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{n \geq 2} \mathcal{N}(C,c)
                  is trivial
          %p
            In particular a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : C \to D
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            if under the nerve it induces a weak equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒩
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒩
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒩
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}(f) : \mathcal{N}(C) \to \mathcal{N}(D)
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
          %ul
            %li
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi 𝒩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 \mathcal{N}(f,c) : \pi_0(C,c) \to \pi_0(D,f(c))
              is an isomorphism implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective functor
              and is implied by
              = succeed "'s" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+functor"} full functor
            %li
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mi 𝒩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1 \mathcal{N}(f,c) : \pi_1(C,c) \to \pi_1(D,f(c))
              is an isomorphism is equivalent to
              = succeed "'s" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
          %h2#references References
          %p Textbook accounts include
          %ul
            %li#GoerssJardine96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rick+Jardine"} Rick Jardine
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simplicial+homotopy+theory"} Simplicial homotopy theory
          %p
            Originally homotopy groups of simplicial sets had been defined in terms of the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} realizing
            them. Apparently the first or one of the first discussions of the purely combinatorial definition is
          %ul
            %li#Kan58
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Kan"}> Dan Kan
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A combinatorial definition of homotopy groups
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1970006?seq=8"} jstor
